title The loop carries the new law before it restarts
prompt Restart the loop, after seating the mechanism-sentence rule.
think A loop restarted against a wall it has never read would meet the mechanism sentence as a refusal rather than as a habit, once per lap, and learn nothing from it. So the prompt carries the law before the run resumes.
think The cellar's own discipline decides how. A filled version is dated testimony and is kept rather than rewritten; the seeds are Tier 3 and may be freshened. So the seed gains one bullet and a fresh dated version is minted, with the elder standing as the record of the hour before.
think Wrote the lift arc's mechanism sentence as a near-template in the new version, since this run's laps are all the same shape -- the N-line body moved into one published function in ladder_checks, each of M rungs calling it through a K-line stub that hands its own type in. A law is easier to keep when the first sentence is already drafted.
obs Named the expected friction honestly in the prompt: 21 of the 40 commits standing at seating read below the floor, so the run will meet the wall early and that is the rule working rather than a fault. A prompt that hides the friction teaches the run to distrust the guard.
loom witness=recursion_prompts_census_witness verdict=green seeds=3
file recursion-prompts/versions/20260822-021339_autonomous-loop-mechanism-first.md the fresh dated version, carrying section 4b and the lift arc's mechanism template
file recursion-prompts/seed/autonomous-loop.seed.md one bullet added to the standing habits, so every future fill inherits the law
recommend keep-going the loop resumes on the Caravan lift arc under the new prompt. First lap hashes may_pass bodies across the 110 modules before writing a line, since note_path proved the queue's rung count is a floor rather than the family, and weighs hand_path at 34 by 27 and seat_the_ground at 43 by 21 against it by realized fall rather than by carried lines.
